WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.140
So there's been a building sort of chorus
of people both on the Trumpy and Right.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:11.599
And also some on the anti Biden left who have
just been insisting that Joe Biden can't possibly

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:12.930
hold it together.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:18.650
In an interview, he can't possibly hold it
together under questioning from reporters.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.690
And we had finally some examples that we can
look at.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:27.390
Joe Biden was interviewed on ABC News over
the weekend alongside his running mate, Kamala

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.390
Harris.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:31.949
This was the first joint interview that they
did, I believe.

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:39.870
And the interview was remarkable in how unremarkable
it was from the standpoint of the hysteria

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:45.200
and the hyperbole and the craziness that we've
become used to under Donald Trump.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.590
It was just like a boring political interview.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:55.579
Joe Biden answered questions and he answered
follow up questions.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:01:00.800
And he sounded like a politician for better
or worse, and was completely coherent like

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:01.800
it would.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:07.939
This would not normally be news, but it's
news when you have people on both sides anticipating

00:01:07.939 --> 00:01:11.700
that Joe Biden would devolve into a stuttering.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:12.700
Yes.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:18.329
He has an actual stutter, incoherent mess,
unable to make any point whatsoever.

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:24.899
And in fact, I enjoyed the interview, not
so much, because I just agree with every policy

00:01:24.899 --> 00:01:29.280
decision that is being made by this platform,
the Biden Harris platform.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:35.950
But because it was just normal and we've been
hoping for normal for so long.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.410
So let's look at some clips here.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:45.479
Is Joe Biden saying he would do a national
shut down or recommend one if public health

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:49.399
officials said it was the right idea for dealing
with coronavirus?

00:01:49.399 --> 00:01:52.079
Remember, it's ultimately up to governors.

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:56.810
What the president can do is recommend and
say, hey, guys, let's all do this.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:03.209
And remember that we still have a raging pandemic,
over 180000 deaths as Donald Trump continues

00:02:03.209 --> 00:02:06.950
to insist we've done and are doing really
well with the virus.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.020
Here is Joe Biden sworn in come January.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.879
And we have corona virus and the flu combining,
which many scientists have said is a real

00:02:14.879 --> 00:02:16.219
possibility.

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:19.250
Would you be prepared to shut this country
down again?

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:24.069
I would be prepared to do it every takes to
save lives because we cannot get the country

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:27.989
moving until we control the virus.

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:32.239
That is the fundamental flaw of this administration's
thinking to begin with.

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:38.360
In order to keep the country running and moving
and the economy growing and people employed,

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.410
you have fixed the virus.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.100
You have to deal with the virus.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.159
So if the scientists say, shut it down, I
would shut it down.

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:47.049
I would listen to the scientists.

00:02:47.049 --> 00:02:52.340
Now, immediately, you had people come out
and say, oh, my God, what a socialist authoritarian.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.909
He wants no country.

00:02:53.909 --> 00:02:55.090
He wants no economy.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.189
He wants no businesses.

00:02:57.189 --> 00:02:58.359
Come on, guys.

00:02:58.359 --> 00:02:59.359
Come on.

00:02:59.359 --> 00:03:00.500
Haven't we learned enough at this point?

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.680
Haven't we seen what happened in other countries
versus in the United States when people wore

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.060
masks and they took social distancing seriously?

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.270
And when you have to shut down sectors of
the economy temporarily, you do it, but then

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:14.920
you're able to reopen.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.219
Biden is not saying any.

00:03:17.219 --> 00:03:20.860
If you're shocked that what Biden's saying,
then then essentially you're saying the whole

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.269
world handled it incorrectly.

00:03:22.269 --> 00:03:24.409
We we handled it correctly.

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:27.569
And we have one of the highest per capita
death rates in the world.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:30.269
Biden is just being sensible.

00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:36.079
This is a medical situation, just a candidate
recognizing that distinguishes them from Donald

00:03:36.079 --> 00:03:37.189
Trump.

00:03:37.189 --> 00:03:39.610
We have to defer to public health and medical
officials.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:40.870
That's it.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.609
That's what we need in this country.

00:03:42.609 --> 00:03:45.349
And people are going crazy about authoritarian
Joe Biden.

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:51.400
Now, on top of that, had we done a two month
coordinated shutdown, meaning essential businesses,

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.939
only everybody wears masks.

00:03:53.939 --> 00:04:00.330
No school back in April or May, we never would
have gotten to where we are today, which is

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:06.980
in an emergency situation with one of the
worst coronavirus responses in the world.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.650
People are reacting to Biden like he's the
outlier.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.610
Biden is just saying, let's do what the rest
of the world figured out months ago.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.720
No more, no less.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:22.530
Then Joe Biden is asked because, again, Trump
has been criticizing Biden for being in his

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:23.530
basement.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.540
Joe Biden was asked, can you win a presidential
election from your house?

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.840
Take a look.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.580
I understand the restrictions have covered
and campaigning in this time, but can you

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.580
win a presidential election from home?

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.860
We will.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:40.620
We're going to follow the science, what the
scientists tell us.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.110
We've been able to travel places where we've
been able to do it in a way that we don't

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:47.150
cause the congregation of large numbers of
people.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:48.240
Look what happens.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.650
What's happened with his his events?

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.150
People die.

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:54.150
People get together.

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:56.310
They don't wear masks that end up getting
cold.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:57.410
They end up dying.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.950
So when you hear the president say this guy's.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:00.720
Afraid to leave his basement.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.840
Guess what?

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.360
I have left my basement.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.870
And but here on the meantime, 500 million
people have watched what I've done out of

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.440
my basement.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:12.550
And guess what, people are listening.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:13.630
People are listening.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:15.300
It's about being responsible.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:20.290
I really think that this is creating controversy
where there is no controversy here.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.990
And what's going to be really interesting
is for three and a half years, we've had this

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.639
narrative from Trump that the fake news media
is all against him.

00:05:26.639 --> 00:05:31.289
All the media is against them except Fox News
and even Fox News sometimes is against them.

00:05:31.289 --> 00:05:34.810
So you've got to go to A.N. to find fair media.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.610
What a lot of people have forgotten.

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:38.090
I have not forgotten it.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:41.590
Is that the myth of the liberal media is a
myth.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:47.759
This is a corporatist media with a pension
for salaciousness and controversy.

00:05:47.759 --> 00:05:53.400
And right away, they are taking hook, line
and sinker every narrative set by Trump here.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.379
They're asking about Biden in his basement.

00:05:55.379 --> 00:05:56.569
Guys, there's a pandemic.

00:05:56.569 --> 00:05:57.629
Biden's being responsible.

00:05:57.629 --> 00:05:58.629
That's it.

00:05:58.629 --> 00:05:59.629
Okay.

00:05:59.629 --> 00:06:02.789
And then they continue to take debate the
bait.

00:06:02.789 --> 00:06:07.540
Corporate media does by asking Biden about
the attacks Donald Trump has been making against

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.250
Biden on his cognitive fitness.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:16.629
Now, I happen to think it's fair when you
have candidates that are in their 70s, Trump

00:06:16.629 --> 00:06:20.050
now mid 70s, Biden closer to 80.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:23.700
It's totally reasonable to ask about cognitive
fitness.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:28.400
But what's fascinating here is that corporate,
supposedly fake news, left leaning corporate

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.440
media, they're taking Trump's bait on every
one of these issues, Biden in the basement

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.370
and now Biden's cognitive fitness.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:40.550
I want to turn to the blistering attacks we've
seen from President Trump just this week alone

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:44.710
on your mental fitness, whether you're up
for the job.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:47.610
His campaign has called you diminished.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:50.070
And I'm curious how you'd respond to that.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:52.530
Watch me, Mr. President.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:53.860
Watch me.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:54.870
Look at us both.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:59.330
What we say, what we do, what we control,
what we know, what kind of shape we're in.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:00.340
Come on.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:05.939
Look, I think it's a legitimate question to
ask anybody over 70 years or whether or not

00:07:05.939 --> 00:07:08.539
they're fit and whether they're ready.

00:07:08.539 --> 00:07:12.110
But I just hoping I can say the American people.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.419
It's a legitimate question to ask anybody.

00:07:14.419 --> 00:07:15.419
Watch me.

00:07:15.419 --> 00:07:16.669
Let's put the attacks aside then.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:19.870
The American people remember Ronald Reagan
was 77 when he left office.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.110
He would be 78 entering office.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:26.820
And you have said yourself that you are a
transition candidate.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.330
Does that mean a one term president?

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.330
What is it?

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.330
No, it doesn't mean so.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.099
You're leaving open the possibility you'll
serve eight years?

00:07:32.099 --> 00:07:33.099
Absolutely.

00:07:33.099 --> 00:07:34.099
OK.

00:07:34.099 --> 00:07:36.259
So Joe Biden handling it perfectly, perfectly
well.

00:07:36.259 --> 00:07:41.569
And I do think much like before the Bernie
Biden debate, you had all these people expecting,

00:07:41.569 --> 00:07:46.480
oh, my God, if Biden's up against Bernie one
on one, Biden's going to collapse.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.480
And of course, he didn't.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.960
And he went on to win the primary.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.380
They were disappointed.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:54.210
And I think they're going to be disappointed
again in debates against Trump if they happen.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:58.990
I don't expect any kind of collapse from Joe
Biden.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.610
Biden also was interviewed by ABC.

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:03.180
Is Robin Roberts asked about choosing Kamala
Harris?

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:06.259
And again, this is not a particularly newsworthy
clip.

00:08:06.259 --> 00:08:09.389
It's just notable that Joe Biden is normal.

00:08:09.389 --> 00:08:13.900
He's able to articulate why he selected Kamala
Harris.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:16.550
He's able to speak in complete compound sentences.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.740
We've just become unaccustomed to a take a
look.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:23.219
There is a connection there that I'm going
to talk more about when it comes to BO and

00:08:23.219 --> 00:08:26.009
and other aspects of family.

00:08:26.009 --> 00:08:31.520
You alluded, Mr. Vice President, about the
fact that you made it clear early on that

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:34.030
you were going to select a woman to be your
running mate.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.160
You select a woman of color.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.910
Did you do that to rally your base?

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:42.210
Did you feel pressure to select a black woman?

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:45.270
No, I didn't feel pressure to select a black
woman.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:48.520
But what I do think and I've said it before
and you've heard me say that probably you

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.330
said on your show with you.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:54.160
Is that the government should look like the
people look like the country.

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:57.640
51 percent of the people in this country are
women.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.680
That expression goes.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.220
Women hold up half the sky.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:06.020
And in order to be able to succeed, you've
got to be dealt in across the board.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:12.520
And no matter what you say, you cannot I cannot
understand and fully appreciate what it means

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:20.790
to walk in her shoes, to be an African-American
woman with an American background, child and

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:21.790
immigrants.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.930
She can't assume exactly what it's like to
walk in my shoes.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:27.850
Well, we do know is we have the same value
set.

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:28.900
And I really mean that.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:32.170
And so it was it was easy for me.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.880
It was an easy decision to make.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:40.320
Although there are enormous number of really
qualified women, I spoke to every single woman

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.660
that was on the list before.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:47.930
And as the day I made the choice before they
was announced, I called every single one of

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:48.930
them.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:50.020
So what was the tipping point?

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:55.980
The tipping point was I was it was the race,
several things, but it just seemed to fit

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:57.850
the closest and the best.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:58.950
I thought I understood.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:06.190
And I think I understand her where she comes
from, what her instincts are, her her character.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:08.780
I watched her take on the Big Bang.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:13.370
I watched her take on the gun lobby, I watched
her the way she was a prosecutor, I've watched

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.410
her as the United States senator.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:20.810
Isn't this so weird that Joe Biden just answers
questions and stays on topic and doesn't ramble

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:23.330
and and again uses compound sentences now?

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:30.700
Then asked whether she still agrees with her
prior call for more police officers on the

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:35.130
streets, which has been really the big liability
for Kamala Harris.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:39.810
She doesn't directly answer, as politicians
often avoid doing.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:45.690
Instead, she praises Black Lives Matter as
important in a national conversation about

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.180
policing.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:51.330
And you know the name that you have, Comilla
top cop and the book that you wrote 10 years

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:57.230
ago, Smart on Crime, where you conclude by
saying that you wanted to see more police

00:10:57.230 --> 00:10:58.230
on the street.

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:00.590
Do you still feel that way?

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.940
Listen, I think that there is no question.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:12.040
First of all, when I wrote that book, We Black
Lives Matter did not exist.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:18.730
And I give full credit to the brilliance of
that movement in terms of what it has done

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:23.120
to advance a conversation that needed to happen
a long time ago.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:31.950
What Black Lives Matter has done as a movement
has been to be a counter force against a very

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:35.190
entrenched status quo around the criminal
justice system in America.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:41.870
And that's why I'm so excited about what we
can do in terms of a new administration in

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:42.870
the White House.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:45.610
Okay, so Kamala Harris is sort of equivocating.

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:48.080
She's saying Black Lives Matter is good.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:52.110
She's saying, well, what I did before was
a while ago.

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:56.790
You can't really explain it any differently
other than to say I was attorney general at

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:59.150
the time and I was doing my job.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:03.000
This is this is standard politics and we don't
have to like it.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:07.440
But again, it's not about whether you accept
Carmella's answer.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:13.490
It's about the reality that these are just
normal people who relate to the media normally,

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:17.860
who relate to their families normally, who
can complete a thought.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:22.450
And that has been so missing for years in
this country.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:25.300
Meanwhile, Donald Trump did not have a very
good week.

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.640
And let's talk about that next

